/-!
# The 28 residuals of `CertSmallerShort` as `IExpr`s

Generated by the Python port script. Each named intermediate `X` of
`SmoothedOctagon.Certificates.SmallerShort.Point` used by these residuals becomes an `IExpr`
definition `r_X`, with the denotation lemma `r_X_den : r_X.denote ρ = (PS ρ).X`,
`PS ρ = ⟨ρ 0, …, ρ 5⟩` (coordinates `r, δ, α, ρ, v, E`).

## The touching point

Numerically, `B₀` contains a point
`x° ≈ (r, δ, α, ρ, v, E) = (0.3196127, 0.0509350, 1.1397991, 0.1021522, 0.7825397, 0.1008571)`
where `f₀, f₂, f₁₁, f₁₂` vanish simultaneously (to `10⁻¹⁴`, by SLSQP maximisation of
`minᵢ fᵢ`) and all of `f₀, …, f₂₂` are `≥ 0` (`f₂₃, …, f₂₆ > 0` there too). Only
`f₂₇ = -excess ≈ -1.3·10⁻³` excludes it, so the cover cannot be certified without the
arctan residual, and a neighbourhood of `x°` dominates the size of any first-order certificate.

## Main API

`PS`, `r_fs` (the residual list), `r_fs_allNonneg`.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option linter.unusedSimpArgs false
set_option linter.unusedTactic false
set_option linter.unreachableTactic false

namespace SmoothedOctagon.Interval.SS

